ANNOUNCEMENT - Linux for Astronomy CDROM  

'The Random Factory' is pleased to announce the production of
a CDROM packed with Astronomical software built for use with the 
'free' operating system -  LINUX. (a U**X clone for i386/486/586
processors).

Finally, it is possible to run the same packages you previously
could use only on expensive workstations. Linux is a full workstation
environment (X-windows, networking, NFS, etc). Thanks to recent
hardware advances, it is even possible to use a laptop computer.

The `Linux for Astronomy' packages cover data processing fuctions
useful in all areas of Astronomy, from pre-processing and enhancing
CCD images, to analysing spectra, and photometric data.

CDROM DETAILS

Price (single issue)  $35.00
Subscription (2 issues per year)  $55.00

The CDROM is formatted using the industry standard ISO9660
format (with RockRidge extensions). The first release contains a
full 650Mb, so future releases may have to be 2-disk sets.


PACKAGES

The following packages are included on the CDROM

		AIPS (radio astronomy and image processing)
		ASSIST (gui for IRAF and other packages)
		glish (distributed processing)
		IRAF V2.10.4 + contributed packages (general purpose)
                                                      ared
                                                      egodata
                                                      finder
                                                      fitsik
                                                      mem0c
                                                      psikern
                                                      rvsao
                                                      tables
                                                      stsdas
		KARMA (image processing)
		NEMO (stellar dynamics)
		MIDAS (general purpose)
		PGPERL (graphics)
                           SAOIMAGE (image display)
		SAOtng (imaging/graphics)
		StarBase (astronomy database)

All packages are the most recent versions available. Subscribers
receive two issues per year to keep their collections up-to-date.


The collection has been assembled with the assistance
of the worldwide astronomical software community. Many of the 
packages may be run directly from the CD, or may be copied
to a local disk for increased efficiency.  The product also contains
software developed by the University of California Berkeley and its
contributors.

Many packages contain general purpose image processing capabilities
which can be used in other subject areas (e.g. medical image
analysis).


DOCUMENTATION

The CDROM  includes an integrated set of documentation
in HTML format, and many packages also includes  .ps
format documents. The documentation is searchable using            
included WAIS tools, and facilities are provided to setup a server to 
provide WWW based searching of the database on your local 
network.

A searchable database cataloguing over 6000 Astronomy related
World-Wide-Web resources is also included.

Source code is  included where permitted by the package license 
holders.

NEW TO LINUX  ?

In case you have not yet experienced the advantages of LINUX, 
the disk also includes a Linux 'test drive' which can be
installed and run directly from MSDOS. 

For  serious use, we recommend you obtain one of the many
cdrom based distributions and dedicate a disk partition to Linux.

 

AVAILABILITY

The single issue cost is $35 (+s&h), and the
CDROM is also available on a subscription basis, 
which is updated twice per year to track new releases
of the main packages ($55 per year + s&h).


