The AdvanSys Linux SCSI Driver is available on our FTP, WWW, and
BBS sites. Just like all of our drivers it supports all AdvanSys
adapters in the same driver. The driver includes support for the
card shipped with the HP SureStore, which is currently the ABP-5150.
The driver was developed and tested on Linux v1.2.1 and v1.3.57.
The BETA version has been used by a number of people for the past
few weeks. There is a patch available for v1.3.57. Linus said he
would include the driver in v1.3.58.

Bob Frey
bobf@advansys.com
  
FTP, WWW, and BBS sites:
 ftp://ftp.advansys.com/pub/linux
 http://www.advansys.com/linux.html
 AdvanSys BBS: 1-408-383-9540 (9600,N,8,1)

Files available:
  linux.txt   Readme File
  linux.exe   DOS self-extracting archive that can be used to create
              a boot diskette. The kernel on the boot diskette is
              configured with the AdvanSys driver. With this diskette
              and a root diskette Linux can be installed using an
              AdvanSys adapter.
  linux.tgz   gzip compressed tar archive containing advansys.h
              and advansys.c. The driver can be added to a system
              after an installation has been done.
  v1_3_57.gz  Patch for the Linux 1.3.57 kernel. If you have a
              v1.3.57 kernel you can execute  the following command
