Mailleds is a tiny daemon that monitors a mailbox, and when the mailbox
contains new mail, blinks the keyboard LEDs.  I find that it's a nice way to
know when you have mail -- it doesn't interrupt whatever you're doing by
posting an on-screen message.  Another benefit of LED mail notification is
that the monitor need not be on to know when mail has arrived.  I can leave
my monitor off all day, and either turn it on or not depending on whether or
not I have mail.

This is my first (and most likely not last) contribution to the Linux
project, so forgive any newbie coding mistakes I have made in the process. 
It started as a shell script, and has made its way through a perl script up
to C, finally.  Having said this, bug reports, comments and patches are
welcome to osheroff@netcom.com (Benjamin Osheroff)

