                        ldlas version 0.8

                ldlas, damned lies, and statistics

Date: January 26, 1996

The first public release of ldlas (ldlas08.tgz), a statistics and 
graphing program, was placed in the Incoming directory at 
sunsite.unc.edu today. It is expected to be moved to moved to 
/pub/Linux/apps/math/ directory.

Highlights include:

        * An ncurses based windowing interface with command line
          editing and command history.

        * On line help.

        * The ability to import data from space delimited ASCII
          files.

        * Graphical output (plotting) to many different file formats
          with various line, point, and titling options.

        * Output tables of data and statistical information in a
          TeX-ready format.

        * Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) regression routine.

        * Statistical summaries including mean, variance, quartiles,
          and histogram plots.

        * Distributed under the GNU General Public License.

        * On line introductory tutorial.

        * .dvi format manual included in A4 and 8.5x11 formats.

        * Distribution includes binary, source, and documentation.


