I am looking for someone interested in writing a Linux display 
driver for the new Cirrus Logic CL-GD5462 graphics accelerator.
It is a very cool chip that uses RAMBUS memory technology and 
has a fast XY based 3 operand accelerator integrated with a 
standard VGA controller and fast back end.  It supports 
resolutions up to 1600x1200, color depths of 8, 16, 24, and
32 bits per pixel, and refresh rates up to 85 Hz.  There is 
also a stretch engine and color space conversion engine for 
video support. 3D will be in the next rev of the chip.

I will supply card(s), Technical Reference Manuals, and help to 
someone who will produce a good Linux dirver for me. I prefer
someone in the Seattle area so that I can see them face to face 
on occasion.  This could lead to a job as a driver writer.

