Hi Folks,

  This is an extra release of the xtoolplaces patch
for adding support for xtoolwait-0.3, by Richard Huveneers.
It actually adds support for many xtoolwait-like tools.
This patch should be applied to the xtoolwait 1.3.1  (or 1.3p3)
package by Adam Stein <adam@iset.scan.mc.xerox.com>.
(which can be found at
    src.doc.ic.ac.uk:/usenet/comp.sources.x/volume19/Xtoolplaces)
Xtoolplaces is a program which saves your X-windows desktop
configuration, so you can restart in the same configuration.
Xtoolwait is a tool that starts an application and waits for
its window to map, and then exits. This improves performance
of your X-session at startup time, when compared to just
starting everything in the background.

Besides adding support for xtoolwait it also fixes some
problems in xtoolplaces 1.3.1.

Originally I released this patch as part of the xtoolwait-0.3
package, but for some reasons (mainly stupidity ;-)) some of the
bug-fixes did not find their way into the patch. Since
there will be no new release of xtoolwait in the near future
I decided to release the patch separately, this time with the correct
bugfixes.

So, here it is, enjoy,
   Peter Bollerman <bollerma@math.ruu.nl>


For details, here is the lsm:

