Info for Prospective CalLUG Guest Speakers:

CalLUG encourages guest speakers at our meetings. If you represent a
company or organization that has valuable information pertinent to the Linux
community and would like to make a presentation at a CalLUG meeting, we ask
that you take these factors into account: 

     CalLUG meetings are generally on Wednesdays around 7:00 pm, though
     meeting dates and times are flexible. 

     CalLUG meetings usually last between 1 and 2 hours, so presentations
     should be kept to around 1 to 1.5 hours. 

     CalLUG members come from all over the Bay Area, though most are
     students, faculty, and staff of the University of California, Berkeley. 

     CalLUG members have varying degrees of experience with Linux.
     Some members haven't even installed it yet, while others have been
     administering a Linux system for years. 

Knowing this, if you think your presentation would be interesting and useful 
to CalLUG members, please mail board@callug.cs.berkeley.edu with: 

     Name of your organization 
     Name of a contact person 
     Email address and phone number of a contact person 
     What your organization does 
     Subject of the presentation 
     Equipment requirements (that you cannot provide) 
     Best time and day of the week 
     Approximate length of presentation 
     Any other information you think we should know 

There are only a limited number of CalLUG meetings every year, and we will
do our best to schedule as many talks as we can that would be of interest to
the largest number of our members. We look forward to hearing from you. 

Thanks,
Paul Eastham
