-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

This is the fifth release of knews, a threaded nntp newsreader
for X.  You can find it at:

http://www.matematik.su.se/users/kjj/knews.html
ftp://ftp.matematik.su.se/pub/kjj/knews-0.9.4.tar.gz

To install it you need an ANSI C compiler, the X libraries of
version X11R4 or greater and an OS supporting POSIX+sockets.


Here are some of the features:

+  True threading, with a graphical tree for the threads.
+  Some features to improve things for people reading over slow lines:
     *  Background threading.
     *  Doesn't have to read the active file.
     *  Caching of thread information.
     *  A mechanism for reading the spooldir.
+  Kill file support, with the ability to mark interesting articles,
   subjects and threads with color blobs.
+  Regular expression searching in articles and the newsgroup list.
+  Different fonts and colors for quoted text and headers in articles.
+  Full support for reading MIME articles, except message/partial.
+  Very configurable.

What's new in 0.9.4?

+  Sorting of the threads.
+  Clicking on URLs.
+  Fast way to add stuff to the kill file.
+  A listing of the groups before posting.
+  Complete reworking of the per server and per group configuration.
+  Many small enhancements, see the CHANGES file for details.

Special thanks to:

J=F6rg Wunsch         The 'pre-post' message is based on his code.
Matthias Schuetze   Icon, new % expansions in attribution.
Joao Cardoso        Assistance in tracking down a bug that caused
                    knews to hang at ~96% of threading sometimes.

- --=20
