I just uploaded fdisk-3.04 to sunsite.unc.edu and tsx-11.mit.edu
and to ftp.win.tue.nl:/pub/linux/util/fdisk-3.04.tar.gz .

It is identical to fdisk-3.03 except that an option has been added
to list the Id of a given partition:
	% fdisk --id /dev/sdb 4
	83
	%

(Distribution maintainers: this version of fdisk is not user-friendly
enough to replace the old fdisk; on the other hand it is useful
enough that one wants to have it. So, on a system that has both
fdisk 2.1 and fdisk 3.04, the latter should probably be called fdisk3.
Once cfdisk 3.* exists, we can throw out the old fdisk.)

