-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

I've just released a new version of xpdf, my Portable Document Format
(PDF) viewer for X.

If you've wanted to look at PDF files, but couldn't because Adobe
didn't have a viewer for your system, you'll want to check out xpdf.

Instructions are included for setting up netscape to run xpdf when you
click on a PDF file link.

Binaries are available for:

* Linux (x86)
* AIX 4.1 (PowerPC)
* SunOS 4.1 (SPARC)
* Ultrix 4.4 (MIPS)
* OSF/1 1.3 (Alpha)

Source (C++ and C) is also available, and it should be fairly easy to
compile for other UNIX / X systems.

This is an alpha version, so it's still a little buggy.

This version contains a workaround for the Unisys LZW patent.
LZW-compressed data is converted (without decompressing) to standard
UNIX compress format, and then uncompress is used to actually do the
decompression.

More information, source code, and precompiled binaries are at:

  http://www.contrib.andrew.cmu.edu/usr/dn0o/xpdf/xpdf.html

The source code is available from:

  ftp://ftp.x.org/contrib/applications/xpdf-0.3.tar.gz

It will also be uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu as soon as I can get
through (check /pub/Linux/Incoming and
/pub/Linux/apps/graphics/viewers).

- - Derek


