started writing a successor.  This is version 0.2 of fe, a new folding
editor.  In contrary to fe 0.1, this version is stable enough for daily
use.

The current release has the following features:

o  Of course folding!
o  regions and Emacs-like kill ring
o  Incremental search
o  Keyboard macros
o  allows editing binary files
o  menues for the most important functions
o  fe is a very small editor
o  reference manual in troff -mm, PostScript, ASCII and HTML

The following things were changed compared to version 0.1:

o  Various bug fixes.
o  On systems without vfork(), fork() will be used.
o  Incremental search works together with the search history.
o  Funtions to delete words and go to matching paren/brace/bracket.
o  Ported to HP-UX
o  Sub shell command added
o  Overwrite mode added
o  Display code prepared for multiple windows
o  Loading files is faster
o  Auto-indent mode added
o  Set language added
o  Origami-style marks at the beginning and end of files
o  Reference manual also available in HTML

fe should work on any system which supports the following:

o  POSIX
o  ANSI C
o  SYSV curses library (ncurses is a free clone)

