- --------------------------------------------------------------

MMAUDIO Evaluation copy Version 0.9.5
=====================================

This is the evalution copy of MMAUDIO, a highly featured audio
player for Unix-systems. The evaluation copy is limited to
playback only. It's main feature is to playback directly
while receiving audio data from a Web-Server !!!
This program belongs to the PowerWeb solution, that
will play any MultiMedia-file in realtime from the Web !

Finally this is the first application with a X11-Interface
supporting encoding and decoding of MPEG-auydio files !

- - supports on Sun's and Linux

        o 8-bit- a/u-law or snd-files
        o G.721 adpcm
        o whatever raw PCM
        o WAV
        o MPEG-1 audio Layer 1&2

- - records and encodes MPEG-audio
- - starts und stops on demand
- - records and plays
- - adjust volumes
- - autodetects AU (u-law/u-law), ADPCM, WAV, MPEG
- - can handle mime types and plays directly from Web-server
  through build-in http-support !


OPTIONS
=======

Command line options:

        -autostart
        -volume/simple/intermediate/complex
        -headphone
        -linein
        -onrepeat
        -bigbuttons
        -path <dir>
        -mimetype <mime-type>
        -verbose
        -recorder
        -viewer (default)
        -geomstr <geometry string>


FULLY REGISTERED VERSION
========================

The fully featured version is already running, but not yet
available to purchase. Stay tuned and look at the Web-page

    http://www.cs.tu-berlin.de/~phade/powerweb

for newer information. The fully featured version
supports recordings and the playing of audio files
bigger than 200 kbyte.


INSTALLATION
============

To install MMAUDIO simply run 'install.sh' from the directory this
README-file is in and give two additional paramters. First, the
directory you like to have the MMAUDIO-start-script to be placed
(usally a directory in your path, f.e. /usr/local/bin), second
the directory you want MMAUDIO's library-files to be placed
(f.e. /usr/local/lib). Not existing directories will be created.

Please give absolut pathnames as parameters, f.e.

	./install.sh /usr/local/bin /usr/local/lib

Furtherone this version depends on the following packages
installed:

	tcl7.4 URL=ftp://ftp.cs.berkeley.edu/pub/tcl/tcl7.4*.tar.gz
	tk4.0  URL=ftp://ftp.cs.berkeley.edu/pub/tcl/tk4.0*.tar.gz
	tix4.0 URL=ftp.cis.upenn.edu/pub/ioi/Tix4.0b4.tar.gz

MMSAVE needs to find the at least the complete tree of
the scripts provided by these packages, please set the
following environment variables to point to the
scripts of the packages.

These are the pre-compiled locations for the Linux-executable:

	setenv TCL_LIBRARY "/usr/tcl/lib/tcl7.4"
	setenv TK_LIBRARY "/usr/tcl/lib/tk4.0"
	setenv TCL_LIBRARY "/usr/tcl/lib/tix"

These are the pre-compiled locations for the Solaris-executable:

	setenv TCL_LIBRARY "/usr/local/tcl/tcl74tk40b3/lib/tcl"
	setenv TK_LIBRARY "/usr/local/tcl/tcl74tk40b3/lib/tk"
	setenv TCL_LIBRARY "/usr/local/tcl/tcl74tk40b3/lib/tix"

Set them to suite your installation ...


