DDD 1.4b Binaries for Linux are available
=========================================

A Linux binary of the Data Display Debugger (DDD 1.4b), a graphical
front-end for GDB and DBX debuggers, has been uploaded to

    ftp://ftp.ips.cs.tu-bs.de/pub/local/softech/ddd/bin/linux/

and will soon be available at

    ftp://ftp.th-darmstadt.de/pub/programming/tools/ddd/bin/linux/
    ftp://ftp.gre.ac.uk/pub/tools/debuggers/ddd/bin/linux/
    ftp://uiarchive.cso.uiuc.edu/pub/packages/ddd/bin/linux/

as well as

    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/devel/debuggers/

and all of sunsite's mirror sites.

This release contains substantial fixes for Linux systems.  If
previous DDD releases failed to run on your system, try this one.

The binary comes in fully statically linked ELF format.  It has been
reported to run without trouble on ELF systems as well as on a.out
systems with compiled-in ELF support.  Most recent a.out systems
include ELF support; other users of Linux a.out systems should compile
ELF support in their kernel.

