-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

I just uploaded man-1.4f to the usual places.
(They will still be in [Ii]ncoming on sunsite and tsx-11.)

It is almost identical to man-1.4e, and English speakers
have no reason to upgrade.

The reason for the change is that the function catopen()
in libc, which functioned according to X/Open specifications
under libc 4.6.27, now [that is, under libc 5.0.9]
no longer looks at the LANG environment variable,
so that on recent systems "LANG=de man foo"
no longer gives messages in German.
(Other programs, like elm, have similar problems.)

The change is to add a private copy of catopen.c.
Hopefully some version of this will find its way into libc.

man-1.4f.lsm:

Begin3
Title:		man
Version:	1.4f
Entered-date:	960107
Description:	A man pager. It has support for compressed pages
		(both man pages and cat pages), and for locale ($LANG)
		and for message catalogs ($LC_MESSAGES). It will format
		files given explicitly (man ./foo.man.gz).
		It conforms to FSSTND, if desired, and handles stray cats.
		This version is almost identical to 1.4e but fixes the
		catopen() that is broken in libc 5.0.9.
