-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

We are pleased to announce that GroupKit version 3.1 is 
available.  If you haven't checked it out in a while, 
you will find many new conferences, some new concurrency
control methods, new programming abstractions, several
new groupware widgets, and more.

If you're not familiar with it, GroupKit allows you to
build real-time groupware tools, such as shared whiteboards,
multi-user games, meeting support tools, and so on.  The
system runs on any Unix system, and uses the Tcl/Tk language
as a basis for building applications.  GroupKit is known for
its easy learning curve, and it comes with over twenty example
groupware applications to get you started.

For more information on GroupKit or any of our other related
groupware projects, please see our WWW page, or just pick up a 
copy of the software from our ftp site (more info on system 
