Meeting Topic: Introduction to Modula-3
		Presented by Farshad Nayeri, GTE Labs
			     Geoffrey Wyant, Sun Microsystems Labs
	
Modula-3 is a language in the Pascal tradition, with a
          freely-available compiler from Digital, featuring:
	+ threads
	+ mutual exclusion
	+ multiprocessor-ready
	+ garbage collection
	+ exceptions
        + objects
        + single inheritance
        + opaque and partially opaque objects
        + encapsulation through the module/interface paradigm
        + genericity at the module/interface level
        + best of all, a reference manual only 56 pages long.


