CLUE Newsletter, December 1995 
==============================

The Colorado Linux Users & Enthusiasts (CLUE), normally meets the
    third Thursday of every month. The next meeting will be at
    7:00pm on December 21st. The location will be Smoky Hill High
    School, located at 16100 E. Smoky Hill Rd. in southeast
    Aurora.

CLUE is for anyone with an interest in Linux, whether you are an
    expert, or just interested and want to know more about the
    Internet and Operating System phenomena that Linux
    represents. All interested parties are invited to attend.
    Let's learn from each other!

For more information, or to be added/removed from the CLUE
    mailing list contact Joel at 303-784-2795 or E-Mail:
    joel@mrg.uswest.com, or attend a meeting, and turn in your
    information there. There is no cost for membership or
    newsletter subscription via E-Mail. 
    
Future Meeting dates will be: 
    Q1/96  January 18, February 15, March 21
    Q2/96  April 18, May 16, June 20

Directions to Smoky Hill High School:  Take Parker south from
    I-225, to Quincy.  There will be a shopping center on the
    left, and a Stoplight. Take a left on Quincy. Then the first
    stoplight with a right turn will be Smoky Hill Road.  Turn
    right onto Smoky Hill, cross Chambers (a light), and then
    turn right at Laredo (a stop light), then left into the
    School parking lot. Go past the main entrance, and to the
    activities entrance.

Vendors are encouraged to attend, make Linux-related
    announcements, etc. WorkGroup Solutions will be giving out
    door prizes at the December meeting.

    Questions and Information: joel@mrg.uswest.com


