This is release 0.1 of cs, a program which is similar to the commercial
cscope(1).  cs indexes C sources and allows interactive queries using the
generated index, which is useful in many situations.  If you frequently
grep for identifiers and edit the found files, then cs is for you.

cs has the following features:

o  find a C symbol
o  find functions called from a certain function
o  find functions calling a certain function
o  find string literals
o  find files #including a certain header file

cs should work on any system which supports the following:

o  POSIX
o  ANSI C
o  SYSV curses library (ncurses 1.9.7 is a free clone)

cs is available via anonymous ftp from cantor.informatik.rwth-aachen.de,
path pub/unix/cs-0.1.tz, packed as GNU zipped tar file.

Michael


