To all the users of taper out there, please note there is a serious bug 
in versions 5.6 to 6.1. 

The bad news:
  There is no way to fix archives that have fallen victim to this bug


The good news:
  It does not occur all the time, but is most likely to occur on slow tape
  drives that have two buffers queued for writing at the end of the backup

  Only the data on the last two blocks of each volume are affected. Since
  a block is typically 28K long, the most you have lost is 56K.


Diagnosis:
  After running mkinfo/check archive, you will be told (in the logfile)
  that the volume count was incorrect and the info file has been fudged
  to overcome it.

The solution:
  Please upgrade to 6.1.1 immediately. Locations:

       sunsite.unc.edu  /pub/Linux/system/Backup (or /pub/Linux/Incoming)
       tsx-11.mit.edu   /pub/linux/sources/sbin



