EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

	Yggdrasil Computing has shipped the world's first video
seminar on installing Linux: "Linux Installation and Beyond."  This
two and a half hour instructional video is available for $24.95 as a
VHS video cassette in NTSC format (the format used in the Americas and
in man industrialized Asian countries).  A PAL version will be
available soon.

	For more information, for the location of an Yggdrasil
reseller near you, or to order directly please call toll free
1-800-261-6630.  If you are a reseller and would like to resell Linux
Installation And Beyond or other Yggdrasil products, please call
1-408-261-6634.


MOTIVATION AND PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

	Installing Linux for the first time can be intimidating, even
for an experienced user.  Seeing the installation of Linux first can
save you time and help you better configure your system.  If you
already have Linux installed, you may find it informative to see the
way someone else has configured their system or to quickly see the
installation of a different Linux distribution without disrupting your
existing system.

	In the past, many people in the silicon valley area have
gotten this over-the-shoulder look at installing Linux by attending
seminars given by Randy Hootman.  Now Randy has condensed his seminars
on installing Linux into a single two and a half hour video: Yggdrasil
Computing's "Linux Installation and Beyond."

	The two and a half hour video seminar begins with a fifteen
minute background of Linux, covering the history of Linux, hardware
requirements, and descriptions of resources commonly used by the Linux
community.  Following this introduction, the main part of the tape
shows the actual installation of three different Linux distributions:

		o Yggdrasil Plug & Play Linux (59 minutes),
		o Red Hat (31 minutes),
		o the free portions of Slackware (46 minutes).

	The video concludes with ten minutes of commonly asked
questions and pointers to additional Linux resources.  Throughout the
video, there are lots of helpful tips and explanations.


SUGGESTED USES

	_Linux Installation and Beyond_ is the first video on
installing Linux.  There has long been a need for an instructional
video that makes Linux accessible to more people and easier to
install.  Here are some suggested uses for Linux Installation and Beyond:

	o NEW USERS can benefit by seeing Linux installations before
	  trying it themselves.

	o PEOPLE ALREADY RUNNING LINUX can use this video to
          familiarize themselves with installation of other Linux
	  distributions without disrupting their existing
 	  installations.

	o Linux Installation and beyond makes a great GIFT for a
	  Linux enthusiast.

	o BUSINESSES.  If you are using Linux or considering using
	  Linux anywhere in a business, distributing copies of this
	  video to your technical staff has got to be one of
	  simplest and most cost effective steps that you can take
	  to increase your technical staff's familiarity and
	  competence with linux.  In addition, the introductory
	  section of this video can be integrated into management
	  presentation about Linux.

	o COURSE MATERIAL.  If you teach a class that is either
	  about Linux or that requires students to install and use
	  Linux to do their assignments, consider adding this video
	  to your course materials list.  This way, students can take
	  home the video and refer to it to get a lot of information
	  that otherwise would have used valuable classroom or
	  instructor time.

