            Free Web Agent CPdog 1.0.0a

CPdog progressively downloads all linked web resources at a given web site.
It also converts absolute URLs in HTML files into relative URLs and
knows if downloaded local copies need to be updated. Thus you don't need
a local server to view your downloaded copies.

It was first written for my wife to follow several daytime soap web sites
through our slow modem link at home.

Now alpha version executables are FREELY available at
anonymous FTP site 
           ftp://kea.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/cpdog/
and a temporary web page
           http://128.149.9.29:8080/cpdog/
Systems supported include Linux 1.2.8, SunOS 4.1.4 and Solaris 2.4.

Source code will also be freely available after it becomes stable.

I WOULD LIKE TO HEAR COMMENTS FROM WEB COMMUNITY SO THAT CPdog CAN BE
IMPROVED AND OFFICIALLY RELEASED IN THE FUTURE.

