-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

There is a critical bug in all releases of safedelete.  The program
safedelchk incorrectly computes the date at which saved files will
be purged.  There is a danger that most, if not all, safedeleted files
will be purged if the patch is not installed.

I've uploaded two files to sunsite.unc.edu. Their filenames are:
safedel-1.2-patch.tar.gz   and   safedel-1.3-patch.tar.gz.  Both files
are in /pub/Linux/Incoming.  Each tar file contains a readme.patch file
and a complete source code replacement for safedelchk.c.

It is highly recommended that safedelchk NOT be used until after the
patch is installed.  If you have problems installing the patch or need a
patch for earlier releases of safedelete just send me a note.

Jeff
